1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. Nf3 e6 7. h4 h6 8. Ne5 Bh7 9. Qh5 Qc7 10. Bc4 Bd6 11. f4 Nf6 12. Qe2 Nd5 13. O-O O-O 14. Nh5 Bf5 15. Bd3 Ne7 16. Rf3 {[White] was already very short of time. The game continued} Bxd3 ({Considerably more interesting, however, are the variations if Black plays} 16... Bxe5 17. fxe5 Bg4 {Aykroyd planned} 18. Rg3 $3 f5 (18... Bxe2 {loses at once to} 19. Rxg7+ Kh8 20. Rh7+ Kg8 21. Nf6#) 19. Nxg7 $3 {and if} Bxe2 {then} (19... Kxg7 20. Rxg4+ Ng6 21. Qe3 {and the attack is too strong}) 20. Nxe6+ {, winning material}) 17. Qxd3 Nf5 18. g4 Nxh4 19. Rh3 Bxe5 20. fxe5 Qd8 21. Bxh6 $1 {and White soon won. Source: CHESS, November 1967, Vol.33/541-2, p49} Ng6 22. Bxg7 Re8 23. Bf6 Qc7 24. Nf4 Nd7 25. Nxg6 Nxf6 26. exf6 Qg3+ 27. Qxg3 fxg6 28. Qd3 Kf7 29. Rh7+ Kxf6 30. Rf1+ Kg5 31. Qe3+ Kxg4 32. Qf4# {Source: Aykroyd scoresheet. Full score contributed by Stephen Wright, 3 June 2025.} 1-0

