{Now for some Aykroyd exploits. He produced another sparkling finish in Round 7, this time with his back to the wall. Gorse (Black) has just played 36...Kf6, the last move before the time control, a truly ghastly move. Instead 36...Rch8 would have given him the superior game. Aykroyd quickly sealed} 37. Rxf4+ $1 {On resumption, the game ended quickly:} ({Stockfish 17:} 37. Be3 $18) 37... gxf4 38. Qf2 Kf7 ({Stockfish 17:} 38... Qh3 $11) 39. Qxf4+ Rf6 40. Qh4 Rf1+ 41. Bg1 Ke8 $2 (41... e6 {resists somewhat longer.}) 42. Rg8+ Rf8 43. Qh8 {Source: CHESS, November 1967, Vol.33/541-2, p49} 1-0

