{This was the position at the adjournment. Wright (White) sealed the correct} 1. Rf2 {Black's reply,} Bxf4 {is forced, and Wright analysed only, and indeed played,} 2. Rxf4+ $2 ({He never noticed that because of the pin, he needn't recapture at once, but could play} 2. Kd4 $1 {and draw in comfort.}) {In the actual continuation, after} 2... Kxe5 3. Rh4 {Drimer played} Rh8 {- clearly the effect of the shock (Source: CHESS, November 1967, Vol.33/541-2, p48, annotated by Andrew P Sombor)} ({and took twice as long to win as after the much stronger} 3... Rc1 {(n.b. Stockfish disagrees with this assessment, preferring ...Rh8 - JS)}) 0-1

