{A tragi-comic incident from Round 10: in this adjourned position, Pedersen (White) was a rook down to Smout. On resumption, after his sealed move,} 37. Qc5+ {, had been made, he offered a draw which Smout rejected. The game continued} Kf7 ({In fact, Pedersen quite genuinely believed that he had a draw by perpetual, and offered the draw mainly for psychological reasons, to indue Smout to play for a win and lose. It seems that neither player had seen} 37... Kd8 38. Rd1+ Rd7 $1) 38. Qc4+ Kf8 39. Qc8+ Ke7 40. Qc5+ Kd7 $2 41. Rd1+ Ke6 $4 ({Even after 41 Rd1+, Smout could have saved himself (and possibly even win) by} 41... Qxd1+ $1) 42. Rd6+ Kf7 43. Qc4+ Kf8 44. Qc8+ Kf7 45. Qe6+ Kf8 46. Rd8# {Source: CHESS, November 1967, Vol.33/541-2, p48 (annotated by Andrew P Sombor)} 1-0

