1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 c6 {"Called the Semi-Slav Defence (the English term was of my christening) Black's opening gets this name from the fact that it is intermediate between the Orthodox Defence characterised by ...e6 and the Slav Defence, characterised by ...c6; Black has played both." (BH Wood)} 4. Nf3 ({"I myself rather favour Marshall's Gambit line} 4. e4 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Bb4+ 6. Bd2 Qxd4 7. Bxb4 Qxe4+ {now, but unfortunately they have found a way for Black to draw against it in the most uninteresting way." (BH Wood)}) 4... Nf6 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 Nbd7 7. Rc1 O-O 8. a3 a6 9. Bd3 Re8 10. h4 dxc4 11. Bxc4 b5 12. Bd3 c5 13. Ne4 cxd4 14. exd4 b4 15. a4 Nd5 16. Nd6 f6 17. Nxe8 fxg5 18. Bxh7+ Kxh7 19. Nxg5+ Kg8 20. Qh5 Bf6 21. Qh7+ Kf8 22. Nxe6+ {Sources: Illustrated London News, 19 August 1967; BCM, September 1967, p260} 1-0

